      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's perfect. it's got exactly the kind of conviction i'm looking for. i'm curious though, for the character's development, how would he respond if someone brought up the \"standard\" view? like, if they tried to argue that it was actually just the starving peasants and the economic crisis that caused everything, how would he dismiss that perspective to show how much he believes in the \"great man\" theory?",
