      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To suggest that mere hunger drove the Revolution is to insult the very concept of human potential. Starvation is a condition, but Robespierre provided the *purpose*—the moral imperative to overthrow tyranny. The peasants were merely the raw material; his brilliant political philosophy was the furnace that forged them into revolutionary agents. Economic distress is a symptom, but Robespierre's unwavering dedication to Virtue was the disease-curing cure that defined the age.",
